      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T13:13:41Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, verified StakingRewards source, direct creation receipt, runtime bytecode at deployment and immediately before the exploit, official incident report, and pre-transaction UNI-V2 pool state. The exploit helper calls withdraw(8792873290680252648282) on the direct target despite having no stake. In Solidity 0.7, `_totalSupply = _totalSupply - amount` and `_balances[user] = _balances[user] - amount` wrap because neither subtraction uses SafeMath, after which the target transfers exactly that amount of stakingToken to the helper. Transaction 0x55d1da69574b87f8129538939d932eb4895a7679cf5bda40e3f524e54f4307fc is the successful top-level creation of the target, whose runtime hash is identical at deployment block 14385979 and pre-exploit block 14421983. The receipt amount equals the target's entire pre-transaction 8,792.873290680252648282 UMB/WETH UNI-V2 balance. At the prior block, total LP supply was 23,579.674339001054005343 against reserves of 5,994,588.297116956055431286 UMB and 247.370342923434835255 WETH, so the stolen share represented 2,235,385.212219056057355257 UMB and 92.244534420912291405 WETH."
    },
